                                                      BUSINESS Question 
How does the churn rate change as customer tenure increases, and which tenure group has the highest churn rate?

                                 Query
SELECT
CASE WHEN Tenure_in_Months BETWEEN 1 AND 12 THEN '1-12 Months'
WHEN Tenure_in_Months BETWEEN 13 AND 24 THEN '13-24 Months'
WHEN Tenure_in_Months BETWEEN 25 AND 36 THEN '25-36 Months'
WHEN Tenure_in_Months BETWEEN 37 AND 48 THEN '37-48 Months'
ELSE '49+'
END AS customers_groups,
COUNT(*) total_customers,
SUM(CASE WHEN Customer_Status ='Churned' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS churn_customers,
ROUND(SUM(CASE WHEN Customer_Status ='Churned' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)* 100.0/COUNT(*),2) AS churn_rate
FROM telecom_customer
GROUP BY CASE WHEN Tenure_in_Months BETWEEN 1 AND 12 THEN '1-12 Months'
WHEN Tenure_in_Months BETWEEN 13 AND 24 THEN '13-24 Months'
WHEN Tenure_in_Months BETWEEN 25 AND 36 THEN '25-36 Months'
WHEN Tenure_in_Months BETWEEN 37 AND 48 THEN '37-48 Months'
ELSE '49+'
END
ORDER BY churn_rate DESC;

                                             INSIGHT:
Churn rate generally decreases as customer tenure increases.


                                        Possible drivers:
Further analysis shows that Customers with shorter tenure, particularly those on month-to-month contracts, showed higher churn rates. 
This suggests that newer customers short term  contracts may be more likely to churn early.

